PRIVATE REFLECTION: The board is
Black A2 B3 B4 C1 C2 ; White B5 C3 C4 D1 D2 D5.
G3 = C1-C2 has L = {B1,B2}
G1 = A2 has L = {A1,A3,B2}
G2 = B3-B4 has L = {A3,A4,B2}
B2 is the common liberty of G1,G2,G3.

W B1. After 1 W B1 G3 is in atari on B2. B B2 is legal. The stone B2 joins A2,B3,B4,C1,C2 into M. L(M) = {A1,A3,A4} and L(W B1) = {A1}. 1…B A3 or 1…B A4 etc loses G3 at once to 2 W B2, so black is forced to 2 B B2. After 2 B B2 white has the two-point net A1/A3/A4 vs B1. Any white A3/A4 is immediately answered by B A1 or B A4 capturing the white net stone and the merged black group keeps ≥2 liberties; W A1 is suicide. No forced capture.

W B2. 1 W B2 puts W B2 and G3 in mutual atari on B1 and leaves G1,G2 with A1,A3,A4. The only legal saving reply is 2 B B1 capturing W B2 and joining B1 to G3. After 2 B B1 L(B1-C1-C2) = {A1,B2}, L(A2) = {A1,A3,B2}, L(B3-B4) = {A3,A4,B2}. W B2 is illegal suicide, W A1 is illegal suicide and any white reduction of A3/A4 is met by B B2 which makes a three-liberty merged group. No forced kill.

W A3. 1 W A3 leaves W A3 with L = {A4}. Black can connect with 2 B B2 giving M with L = {A1,A4,B1} and W A3 L = {A4}, or 2 B B1 giving G3+B1 L = {A1,B2}. In both lines white A4 puts at most one liberty on M and black can answer with A5 capturing the white A3-A4 net, or B B2 to re-connect to L = {A1}. The same mutual atari / capture exchange appears for A4,A1. No first move gives white a legal atari that black cannot answer with B B2/B B1 or a capture of the attacking stone.

The suicide claims for B B2 after W B1 and for B B1 after W B2 are wrong: the connecting move makes a merged black group with liberties A1,A3,A4 resp. A1,B2, so the connecting replies are legal. Hence B1,B2 are not forced kills and A3/A4 are not forced kills either. D3 is a self-preservation move, not a killing move. The board contains no first white move that forces a capture against best defence.

